{"agent_id":"pp3g-7qQf-read-today-s-sessions-to-recover-context-for-session","agent_seq":4,"timestamp":"2026-08-28T12:47:07.410383664Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"c1c2b4e8-0df8-4f2d-a0b8-dbad6c1a6e5f","title":"Feature: session-start model cost-vs-suitability recommender (join opencode models + Routing Matrix)","description":"Goal: \n\nAcceptance criteria:\n- \n\n## Context (WHY)\n\nSESSION-START.md already instructs agents to (a) consult the Model Routing Matrix to pick a model by task type / review lens / token cost (line 9), and (b) verify the live catalog with `opencode models <provider>` before any launch (§1a, lines 74-86). These are two separate *manual* steps. The discussion (captured in #515 after a Crosslink bug blocked the earlier attempt) proposed closing the gap: at SESSION-START, automatically RUN `opencode models <provider>` and JOIN the live catalog with `docs/research/registry/Model-Routing-Matrix.md` to emit a per-task CHEAPEST-SUITABLE model recommendation.\n\nCorroborating evidence from today's model-evidence knowledge pages (model-evidence-2026-08-27-lexicon.md, model-evidence-brief-note.md): cost-vs-suitability is already an active decision axis. muse-spark Zen free = zero cash, 5-10m ceilings, held cadence; hy3 paid = deep re-derivation but token-heavy and subject to silent DEAD-UNMARKED loss; the routing recommendation was \"keep muse-spark Zen as primary builder for 15-20m research synthesis, reserve hy3 for deep source re-derivation.\" The Failure-Matrix (2026-08-18) lists \"model-catalog staleness (Tools #4)\" as a recurring failure class — which is exactly why a live `opencode models` pull at session start matters (models.dev LAGS the Zen API; IDs change).\n\n## What it does\n\n- At session start (or on demand), query `opencode models opencode` and `opencode models opencode-go` (live catalog; models.dev lags the Zen API, so the live pull is authoritative).\n- Join catalog availability against the Routing Matrix's per-model dimensions: Token cost profile, Strengths by task-type, Blind spots, Failure modes, Confidence+evidence.\n- Emit an advisory: for the task type at hand, the cheapest model that is SUITABLE (meets task-type strength + acceptable failure-mode risk), with the runner-up and the cost tier delta.\n\n## Existing foundations (reuse, don't rebuild)\n\n- SESSION-START.md line 9 + §1a (model verification rules).\n- docs/research/registry/Model-Routing-Matrix.md — already dimensioned with cost + suitability.\n- model-discipline.md — Go(paid) vs Zen(free) rules; rule #5 \"if operator hasn't specified a model, ASK — never assume.\"\n- Failure-Matrix.md — \"model-catalog staleness (Tools #4)\" recurring failure class motivates the live pull.\n\n## Scope\n\n- ADVISORY ONLY. The recommender prints a suggestion; it must NOT auto-select or override an operator-named model (model-discipline rule #5). Operator choice remains authoritative.\n- Covers both providers (opencode-go paid, opencode Zen free) and respects the standing facts (no OpenRouter; Google via Vertex; grok forbidden; kimi-k3 expensive-caution).\n\n## Open questions (to resolve in implementation)\n\n1. Form factor: (a) printed advisory block in SESSION-START output, (b) a small script/tool (`scripts/session-model-recommend` or a crosslink/knowledge helper), or (c) a knowledge-page render. Recommend (b) invoked by SESSION-START.\n2. Matrix maintenance: who keeps Routing-Matrix ↔ live catalog join current as model IDs churn? Propose a periodic refresh + a staleness warning when `opencode models` returns an ID not in the matrix (or vice versa).\n3. Task-type detection: how does the recommender know the task type at session start? Options: operator passes it, or it reads the active issue labels (#515 is `research`; builder tasks differ from reviewer tasks).\n\n## Deliverables\n\n- A recommender implementation (script/tool) that performs the join and prints cheapest-suitable per task type.\n- SESSION-START.md update wiring the step in (advisory).\n- A maintenance note: refresh cadence + staleness warning, filed against #255's OPERATIONAL DATA item.\n- Evidence: a dry-run on a real dispatch showing the recommendation vs the model actually chosen.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- Running the step lists, per task type, cheapest-suitable model + runner-up + cost tier, sourced from live `opencode models` + Routing Matrix.\n- Output is advisory; operator-named model is never overridden.\n- Staleness warning fires when catalog/matrix disagree.\n\n## Parent rationale\n\nSub-issue of #255 (EPIC: EDASES Model Data Collection) — item (4) MODEL ROUTING MATRIX \"routing recommendations derived from the evidence\" and item (6) OPERATIONAL DATA. NOT #418 (resolved diagnostic on SESSION-START.md injection mechanism). See #515 for the recovered discussion.\n\n## References\n\n#515 (research issue / recovered discussion), #255 (parent epic), #418 (related but not parent), model-discipline.md, docs/research/registry/Model-Routing-Matrix.md, docs/research/registry/Failure-Matrix.md, model-evidence-2026-08-27-lexicon.md, model-evidence-brief-note.md.","priority":"medium","parent_uuid":"bff799f6-9339-459b-98e7-1a26cd5d29b1","created_by":"pp3g-7qQf-read-today-s-sessions-to-recover-context-for-session"},"signed_by":"SHA256:MSyYepq43o8c1jQL7ayms3hEcLUtV2nZ/CKCkdDoRVs","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgtb/ymHP7ROiXJ5cgXHLOzX3PvrdFt7EwGIISCpVDdYkAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQMRDspXQ4srF7s1xW6qaCJ5dbkYfigWxXjexIGesMHkLDB6aq6S5V+v8CXO+ZR3O9+QR7nRBPJfugOP4BOuyKgg="}
