{"agent_id":"pp3g-7qQf-read-today-s-sessions-to-recover-context-for-session","agent_seq":8,"timestamp":"2026-08-28T12:48:05.214313312Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"ff08a85a-10dc-4c2e-9539-a8d3209b46dc","comment_uuid":"c2dcfba1-7289-44ee-9794-31c3e4041ca6","author":"pp3g-7qQf-read-today-s-sessions-to-recover-context-for-session","content":"## Summary — session-start model cost vs suitability (recovered context)\n\n**What was discussed (reconstructed).** The proposal — captured in #515's own description after a Crosslink bug blocked the earlier attempt, and corroborated by today's model-evidence knowledge pages — is: at SESSION-START, automatically RUN `opencode models <provider>` and JOIN the live catalog with `docs/research/registry/Model-Routing-Matrix.md` (cost vs suitability) to recommend the CHEAPEST SUITABLE model per task.\n\nThis is an EXTENSION of two already-standing rules, not a new concept:\n- SESSION-START.md line 9: \"Model routing: before dispatching agents, consult the Model Routing Matrix ... to pick the model by task type, review lens, and token cost.\"\n- SESSION-START.md §1a (lines 74-86): \"verify the model catalog yourself. `opencode models` is an allowed command ... Run `opencode models opencode` (Zen free) and `opencode models opencode-go` (paid Go) to confirm a model ID exists.\"\n\n**Cost-vs-suitability is already a live decision axis (evidence).** model-evidence-2026-08-27-lexicon.md: muse-spark Zen free = zero cash, 5-10m ceilings, held cadence; hy3 paid = deep re-derivation but token-heavy and subject to silent DEAD-UNMARKED loss; routing recommendation \"keep muse-spark Zen as primary builder for 15-20m research synthesis, reserve hy3 for deep source re-derivation.\" The Routing Matrix already carries a per-model \"Token cost profile\" (LOW/HIGHER/HIGH/LOW-Moderate) + \"Strengths by task-type\" + \"Failure modes.\" The missing piece is the JOIN: turning the static matrix into a per-task cheapest-suitable recommendation at session start. The Failure-Matrix (2026-08-18) lists \"model-catalog staleness (Tools #4)\" as a recurring failure class — direct motivation for the live `opencode models` pull (models.dev LAGS the Zen API; IDs churn).\n\n**Parent recommendation: #255, NOT #418.**\n- WHY: The substance is model-routing / cost-suitability operationalization. #255 (EPIC: EDASES Model Data Collection) explicitly owns item (4) \"MODEL ROUTING MATRIX — the routing recommendations derived from the evidence\" and item (6) \"OPERATIONAL DATA — per-model operational findings ... recorded as first-class.\" A session-start cost-suitability recommender is the operationalization of the routing matrix → squarely #255.\n- WHAT: #418 is \"Diagnose dead instructions wiring: SESSION-START.md not injected in OpenCode 2\" — a resolved diagnostic about the MECHANISM of injecting SESSION-START.md, not its content/model-selection logic. The new feature modifies SESSION-START content but its home is the routing-matrix domain, not the injection-diagnostic domain.\n- HOW-CERTAIN: High (evidence-based from #255 body, #418 body, SESSION-START content).\n- WHAT-NOT-TESTED: did not ask the operator to confirm parent preference; re-parenting is cheap if they disagree.\n\n**What I could NOT recover (honest disclosure).** The operator-referenced \"crosslink sessions #35/#34/#33\" are stale CLOSED E2E kickoff tests (laguna/ling) — not the discussion; the reference was misremembered. The previous research-session-start-model-cost agent was DEAD-UNMARKED (OBSERVER note on #515) with its worktree preserved but no draft summary survived in the tree (only crosslink hydration ref changed). The opencode session EXPORTS for 2026-08-27/28 are session-index metadata only (titles/timestamps), not message transcripts; the actual discussion text is not present in opencode.log beyond the #515 creation command itself. So the recovered \"discussion\" = #515's description + today's model-evidence pages + the standing docs — which together fully specify the proposal.\n\n**Proposed issue spec — created as sub-issue #516 (under #255), related to #515.** Full spec (context, what-it-does, foundations, scope=advisory-only, open questions, deliverables, acceptance criteria, parent rationale, references) is on #516. Key constraints baked in: ADVISORY ONLY (must not override an operator-named model per model-discipline rule #5); covers both providers; staleness warning when catalog/matrix disagree.","created_at":"2026-08-28T12:48:05.207179735Z","kind":"result","signed_by":"SHA256:MSyYepq43o8c1jQL7ayms3hEcLUtV2nZ/CKCkdDoRVs","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgtb/ymHP7ROiXJ5cgXHLOzX3PvrdFt7EwGIISCpVDdYkAAAARY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWNvbW1lbnQAAAAAAAAABnNoYTUxMgAAAFMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAABAx3vK77chTquyEZXvO0PoPa51L0iN4euuIlzT/2GcBIwm7MNH8MlvbNPnEbp9vXjAPjcLw5w13kZnw9TifG3uCw=="},"signed_by":"SHA256:MSyYepq43o8c1jQL7ayms3hEcLUtV2nZ/CKCkdDoRVs","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgtb/ymHP7ROiXJ5cgXHLOzX3PvrdFt7EwGIISCpVDdYkAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQO3ATuYOoioS73R8KLkR3ZFKzEgb5s0xFDBEAw3TUrdtzuEolIBfKVy+t3xqe0b0a+pF52rHciI3X7BwIQ6M4ww="}
